The derived material is the ROM assembly data in `alttpr-fxpak`: the cosmetic
byte offsets and their value tables (heart speed, heart color, menu speed,
music, quickswap, reduce flashing, MSU-1 resume), the sprite injection offsets
and file-select author character maps, the SNES header checksum routine, and
the file-select item code table. These were adapted from pyz3r's `rom.py` and
`alttpr.py`.

Changes from pyz3r: the tables and routines were reorganised into this
project's own Rom class and constants, the heart-color offsets were collapsed
into a loop, and the sprite author character maps are generated from their
alphanumeric ranges rather than written out entry by entry. The BPS patch
applier in this project is an independent implementation written from the BPS
format specification; pyz3r delegates that work to the separate `bps` package.
